  "aim": {
    "cw": "Secure Sollum, then assemble the 6th Australian Division and 7th RTR west and south of Bardia for the 3 January assault. Screen the fortress without launching the main attack early.",
    "axis": "Hold Bardia while withdrawing frontier troops into its perimeter and keeping the Tobruk road open."
  },
  "about": "Research-only linked interval, 17 December 1940 to 2 January 1941. It must continue a played Compass opening. Existing formations and stocks carry forward; copied starting placements and owners below are checker placeholders and are not a historical standalone 17 December deployment. Australian formation arrival dates follow the official history, but entry hexes, strengths, lift, stocks, Sollum landing capacity and combat readiness are game estimates. The existing engine cannot represent temporarily unserviceable tanks, water shortages, naval bombardment, tactical perimeter posts or the detailed assault preparation. Do not read this as a validated Bardia simulation. The Italian XXIII Corps and Blackshirt counters are introduced on 17 December as a model of a pre-existing Bardia garrison; their listed manpower is not a historical strength return. The two staging hexes are approximate 10 km assembly sectors; they direct preparation but do not claim the exact 1:50,000 start line. Tobruk’s pre-existing Italian XXII Corps and Sirte garrison are carried from this chapter so a later campaign handoff never spawns defenders retroactively. The 8,000/6,400 men, 72 guns, and town fort level are game estimates; they are not a reconstruction of the roughly 25,000-man, 220-gun January garrison.",
  "sources": {
    "W": "Wavell, Western Desert operations despatch, London Gazette 37628, sections 10–21: plan, forces, opening, Nibeiwa and Sidi Barrani",
    "P": "Playfair et al., The Mediterranean and Middle East, vol. I, chapter XIV: positions, supply preparation, assault sequence and withdrawal of 4th Indian Division",
    "A": "Australian official history, To Benghazi, chapter 6: Commonwealth formations and armoured screening task",
    "E": "Game estimate: individual-unit strength, exact 10 km placement, opening stock or supply setting not verified by the cited account",
    "B": "Australian official history, To Benghazi, chapter VII Before Bardia: 16th Brigade via Buq Buq and Sollum 17-19 December; 17th Brigade and divisional HQ move ordered for 22 December; 19th Brigade forward 1 January",
    "P2": "Playfair et al., The Mediterranean and Middle East, vol. I, chapter XV: Sollum port and supply, Bardia perimeter preparations, ammunition delay and 7th RTR serviceability",
    "T": "Australian official history, To Benghazi, chapter 9: XXII Corps, 61st Sirte and Tobruk garrison; approximately 25,000 men and 220 guns estimated 15 January"
  },
